ttps://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3252086642/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":5,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3255446327","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-3255446327","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":3255446327,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CCis3","user":{"login":"Jojo-1000","id":33495614,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDk1NjE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33495614?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000","html_url":"https://github.com/Jojo-1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T20:12:48Z","updated_at":"2025-09-04T20:12:48Z","body":"I looked at the code and there are two places that handle the auto advance. Both of them explicitly check and exclude the case that the next clip has the same index as the currently active one. If I just remove that code, the whole playback breaks, so there seems to be a reason for this.\n\nWould it be a viable fix to disable this selection (so that it would be empty with just one clip) and instead enable loop on the audio stream itself (if you open up the import options of the file it has a loop mode)?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3255446327/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3256638834","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-3256638834","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":3256638834,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CHF1y","user":{"login":"alejandro-alzate","id":57909935,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3OTA5OTM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57909935?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate","html_url":"https://github.com/alejandro-alzate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-05T01:00:00Z","updated_at":"2025-09-05T01:00:00Z","body":"Yeah what's up with that, why we cant poke at fields of the streams?\nWhat's the technical reason for that?\nIt got me curious.\n\nWhat is the point of \"transition on next bar/beat\" if the bpm can't be set?\n\nand I have an idea, currently the `finished` signal is dead.\nwhat about reusing it for when a transition is about to happen?\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3256638834/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3256671226","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-3256671226","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":3256671226,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CHNv6","user":{"login":"alejandro-alzate","id":57909935,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3OTA5OTM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57909935?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate","html_url":"https://github.com/alejandro-alzate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-05T01:07:20Z","updated_at":"2025-09-05T01:07:20Z","body":"> I looked at the code and there are two places that handle the auto advance. Both of them explicitly check and exclude the case that the next clip has the same index as the currently active one. If I just remove that code, the whole playback breaks, so there seems to be a reason for this.\n\nRegarding this insight, if a check is explicitly made on this scenario what's stopping us of putting the equivalent of `stop()` then `play()` Back to Back or just `seek(0)` there?\n\nMaybe because I'm incompetent with C-derived languages and I'm probably grasping how the `AudioStreamInteractive` works completely wrong but surely there's a way isn't it?\n\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3256671226/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3257927267","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-3257927267","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":3257927267,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CMAZj","user":{"login":"Jojo-1000","id":33495614,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDk1NjE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33495614?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000","html_url":"https://github.com/Jojo-1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-05T10:50:03Z","updated_at":"2025-09-05T10:50:03Z","body":"> Yeah what's up with that, why we cant poke at fields of the streams?\nWhat's the technical reason for that?\nIt got me curious.\n\nYou can turn on looping and maybe other settings as well if you click on the audio file and go to the import settings (hidden behind the node tree for me).\n\n> Regarding this insight, if a check is explicitly made on this scenario what's stopping us of putting the equivalent of stop() then play() Back to Back or just seek(0) there?\n\nIt would certainly be possible to fix this, but there is quite complex transition logic that relies on a from-state and a to-state for fading and stuff. The assumption is that these states are separate, which breaks in this scenario.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3257927267/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3258349342","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-3258349342","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":3258349342,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CNnce","user":{"login":"alejandro-alzate","id":57909935,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3OTA5OTM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57909935?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate","html_url":"https://github.com/alejandro-alzate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-05T13:24:42Z","updated_at":"2025-09-05T13:24:42Z","body":"> You can turn on looping and maybe other settings as well if you click on the audio file and go to the import settings (hidden behind the node tree for me).\n\nI for the love of god didn't found where to look","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3258349342/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3259154513","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-3259154513","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":3259154513,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CQsBR","user":{"login":"Jojo-1000","id":33495614,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDk1NjE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33495614?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000","html_url":"https://github.com/Jojo-1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-05T17:05:14Z","updated_at":"2025-09-05T17:05:14Z","body":"@alejandro-alzate I don't know if you found it or not, this is where I could change the loop mode:\n\n<img width=\"500\" height=\"1005\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/70d1b9e0-6038-4744-8b11-8ef71f0b46b1\" />\n\nIf you change this to forward and reimport, it will loop without the auto advance.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3259154513/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3262617340","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-3262617340","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":3262617340,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Cd5b8","user":{"login":"alejandro-alzate","id":57909935,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3OTA5OTM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57909935?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate","html_url":"https://github.com/alejandro-alzate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-alzate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-06T16:57:20Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T16:57:20Z","body":"@Jojo-1000\nI'm currently using ogg.\nI'm forced to use WAV?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3262617340/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3263540188","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-3263540188","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":3263540188,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Chavc","user":{"login":"ultigonio","id":59210738,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MjEwNzM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59210738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio","html_url":"https://github.com/ultigonio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-07T06:53:49Z","updated_at":"2025-09-07T06:53:49Z","body":"No, .ogg can be looped just fine as well. It even offers some options that .wav does not.\n\n<img width=\"275\" height=\"680\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/95b6c535-d327-41db-8470-448868b07cd2\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3263540188/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3268959192","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-3268959192","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":3268959192,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7C2FvY","user":{"login":"Etherkin","id":156987767,"node_id":"U_kgDOCVtxdw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/156987767?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Etherkin","html_url":"https://github.com/Etherkin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Etherkin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Etherkin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Etherkin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Etherkin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Etherkin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Etherkin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Etherkin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Etherkin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Etherkin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-09T05:44:55Z","updated_at":"2025-09-09T06:26:33Z","body":"@Jojo-1000 Unfortunately, although it's possible to enable looping in the import settings, this option does not allow us to use any of the transitions that are the reason for wanting to use AudioStreamInteractive (and the amazing flexibility it offers!) in the first place. Looping clips with a cross-fade is common practice. Unfortunately, it seems transitions do not take effect when the stream loops as set in its import settings.\n\n<img width=\"564\" height=\"59\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a538ce08-d8f4-4e0e-9d14-b8308cb9da6e\" />\n\nThe fact that there is a [to] and [from] option for each clip in relation to itself, as well as the option to set the same clip for Auto Advance, made me believe that auto-loops were supported. As of now, the only workaround is the one proposed by @alejandro-alzate, which duplicates every clip that needs to loop _[edit: Wait are the duplicate clips really playing at the same time? That is very strange! In that case, it's just going to cause more bugs...]_.\n\nIf the transitions were to take effect when a clip loops, that would also solve the problem (as well as allow us to set a custom loop start and end time, which would not be possible with AudioStreamInteractive even if Auto Advance worked properly.) In any case, as of now, being able to fade in/out when looping makes a huge difference, so the import setting are not comparable to what AudioStreamInteractive offers.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3268959192/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3271630134","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-3271630134","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":3271630134,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7DAR02","user":{"login":"Jojo-1000","id":33495614,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDk1NjE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33495614?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000","html_url":"https://github.com/Jojo-1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-09T17:21:12Z","updated_at":"2025-09-09T17:21:12Z","body":"> Unfortunately, it seems transitions do not take effect when the stream loops as set in its import settings.\n\nI would say this is expected, as the looping happens one layer \"deeper\", so to the player it looks like an endless clip.\n\n> The fact that there is a [to] and [from] option for each clip in relation to itself, as well as the option to set the same clip for Auto Advance, made me believe that auto-loops were supported.\n\nIf you find an old version where this worked, that would be helpful (I don't think there was from the code history). I have to say that I did not write this code and from what I saw it would be a bit of work to fix this. \n\nYou make a good argument for why it *should* work, though, so I think just disabling the option wouldn't be good enough.\n\n> Wait are the duplicate clips really playing at the same time? That is very strange! In that case, it's just going to cause more bugs\n\nIf it causes bugs even when the clips are added separately (and this isn't just a visual thing), then this might be impossible without also changing AudioStream as well. It would be nice if someone could check that transitions are correct with this workaround.\n\nI am away this week, maybe I can invest some more time next week. Unless someone who is more familiar wants to take a look.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3271630134/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3293755484","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-3293755484","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":3293755484,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EUrhc","user":{"login":"Jojo-1000","id":33495614,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDk1NjE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33495614?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000","html_url":"https://github.com/Jojo-1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jojo-1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-15T20:13:30Z","updated_at":"2025-09-15T20:13:30Z","body":"I tried to implement a fix today, but there is an issue with the way it works internally. Each clip can only play from one position at a time, therefore fading from the same clip to itself is not possible unless I internally replicate the same setup that was presented as a workaround.\n\nEssentially, I would need to duplicate the audio playback instance internally and just hide it from the UI. To make things worse, as transitions can be added dynamically, this would need to happen always and for all clips, or it could cause lags when doing it on demand.\n\nIMO it would be better to make this explicit to the user by disabling the selection and having the user do this double setup if they really need it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3293755484/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4533736145","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-4533736145","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":4533736145,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDjtS0Q","user":{"login":"Thinh-T-Diep","id":57164963,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MTY0OTYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57164963?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep","html_url":"https://github.com/Thinh-T-Diep","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-25T11:01:58Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T11:05:52Z","body":"I know this is an old thread, but I want to contribute to the discussion since as far as I can tell, this problem is still presented in Godot 4.6.3 stable.\n\nIn the workaround, the sound clips are playing at the same time by the AudioStreamPlayer because as AudioStreams, they are Resources in Godot, and Resources by default is one same instance unless \"Made Unique\". It's no different from like a StyleBox or a Shader Material etc. This by itself shouldn't be a source for bugs. If you want to stop the clips from playing at the same time, simply right-click on one of the clips and choose \"Make Unique\" in the drop-down menu, but this will trigger a warning in the editor because the .tscn file will have a large file size.\n\nAnother perhaps slightly \"better\" workaround, if you want to loop the same piece of music clip, is to slice the music into 2 halves, and then stitch them together in the AudioStreamInteractive. In the first half, you can transition without fading into the second half, and at the end of the second half, transition back to the first half with fading.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4533736145/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4536685393","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-4536685393","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":4536685393,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDmhTUQ","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-25T19:27:43Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T19:27:43Z","body":"May I ask why would you want to auto-advance to the same clip instead of enabling looping?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4536685393/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4538810551","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-4538810551","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":4538810551,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDojAtw","user":{"login":"Thinh-T-Diep","id":57164963,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MTY0OTYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57164963?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep","html_url":"https://github.com/Thinh-T-Diep","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thinh-T-Diep/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T01:25:09Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T01:25:09Z","body":"> May I ask why would you want to auto-advance to the same clip instead of enabling looping?\n\nMost common use case is when you want to loop a non-looping audio clip or song, in which case what's usually done is fade out or crossfade the end and the beginning of the clip, so it's not jarring and sudden. If using the looping tag in Import settings, it will loop immediately.\n\nThere's some other considerations as said by some others in the replies above, such as getting a \"finished\" signal emission when an audio clip finishes. If enabled looping in Import, it will not emit the \"finished\" signal ever.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4538810551/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4540557943","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-4540557943","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":4540557943,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDqNqdw","user":{"login":"ultigonio","id":59210738,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MjEwNzM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59210738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio","html_url":"https://github.com/ultigonio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T05:34:35Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T05:45:41Z","body":"> May I ask why would you want to auto-advance to the same clip instead of enabling looping?\n\nOh, I've actually got a very specific use-case I can point to. \n\n<img width=\"1000\" height=\"312\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/613a6928-15be-43c0-835c-e57d10a51c39\" />\n\nSo basically what you're seeing here is one of the loops we iterated through for a dynamically-scored cutscene in our game - except, it's not actually a traditional loop. You can see that it fades out, right? This is because it actually ends in a reverb tail. Because of this reverb tail, when each track transitions to the next one, it doesn't feel like the song abruptly starts from 0 all over again - the reverb from the previous section of music is able to carry over for a more natural-sounding result. However, this reverb tail obviously means that we can't loop the audio traditionally, so we'd need to be able to loop the clip from partway, and then allow its reverb tail to play over itself when looping. If the AudioStreamInteractive were able to auto-advance a clip to itself, this would have been fine, but because it's not, it ended up being a bit of a headache.\n\nI _was_ ultimately able to work around this, but it was extremely scuffed - I had to duplicate every clip and then ping-pong back and forth between the duplicate clips at times when I wanted them to loop (I think this is what is noted above, as well?). This setup was really not intuitive and probably cost me a good few hours just trying to figure out what my options even were.\n\nFor reference, that system in action:\nhttps://youtu.be/PdqgYFNGIPA?t=66\n\nPerhaps a more seasoned Godot expert would happen to know a way to accomplish this without auto-advancing clips to themselves? But I didn't really see a better way. A lot of games do this sort of dynamic scoring, so being able to easily implement the same in Godot would be wonderful. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4540557943/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4594091915","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110216#issuecomment-4594091915","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110216","id":4594091915,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEdRHiw","user":{"login":"mgjv","id":839370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzOTM3MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/839370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgjv","html_url":"https://github.com/mgjv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgjv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgjv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgjv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgjv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgjv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgjv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgjv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgjv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgjv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-01T15:33:23Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T15:33:23Z","body":"I was also looking for the same thing here. It is quite normal for background music to 'loop' in games. It is really odd that there isn't simply a 'loop' option on each clip. The implementation where you transition to yourself is not the right one, even if you disregard the technical problems with that. It should simply start playing the stream from the start when the stream finishes. Even factually firing the finished signal when a stream hits the end would be sufficient for us to work around this.\n\nImplementing the above workarounds to me feels like a lot of work. I've switched back to tweening the volume on two regular streams. Quite simple. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4594091915/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]